SUMMARY:Stand Up Comedy: Orlando Baxter | 8:00PM Show
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 29 spots left\nS
 tatus: You are on Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/203607\n\nOrlando Baxter brings his sharp\, deeply relatable comedy t
 o The ’House for an evening of stand-up inspired by family\, relationshi
 ps\, work\, and the everyday absurdities of life. A former public high sch
 ool teacher\, Orlando spent 12 years in the classroom—an experience that
  continues to shape his quick wit\, natural storytelling\, and unmistakabl
 e point of view.\n\nSince trading lesson plans for the stage\, Orlando has
  entertained audiences around the world\, appeared on Conan\, and earned 
 more than five million views for his comedy special\, Glorified Baby Sitt
 er.\n\nEnjoy a pre-show cocktail from the cash bar before settling in for 
 the performance. Seating is first come\, first served.\n\nMake a night of 
 it with a burger and beer in The Pub before the show. Dining walk-ins are 
 welcome.\n\n*This event is available for members and up to one registered 
 guest. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kind
 ly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start
  of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203607
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-203633@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260930T183000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T200000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: How Hip-Hop Built an Empire
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 11 spots left\nS
 tatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/203633\n\n6:30PM Reception\, 7:00PM Discussion\n\nWhat is it about hip-
 hop that has transformed generations of artists into some of the world’s
  most influential entrepreneurs\, tastemakers\, and cultural forces? Join 
 us for a ’Quin Chat exploring the evolution of the hip-hop artist from p
 erformer to mogul - and how a genre born from creative expression has beco
 me a powerful engine for business\, innovation\, and cultural influence. F
 rom fashion and record labels to food and beverage\, technology\, media\, 
 and beyond\, the conversation will examine how artists have built expansiv
 e ecosystems around their creativity while reshaping the industries they e
 nter. \n\nNeil Martinez Belkin\, New York Times bestselling author\, wi
 ll be joined in conversation by Boston native Dart Adams\, an acclaimed jo
 urnalist\, historian\, researcher\, lecturer\, and author. Together\, the
 y will explore the entrepreneurial mindset behind hip-hop’s most influen
 tial figures\, the relationship between cultural credibility and commercia
 l success\, and how the genre continues to redefine what it means to be an
  artist\, and a mogul\, today.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserve
 d for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be ser
 ved. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior 
 to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203633
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
